**Childcare cost creep (your biggest real risk)** — At SGD 25K income, CHAS/Baby Bonus subsidies are reduced. Full-cost childcare for 2 kids: SGD 1,400–2,400/mo. International schooling (if planned): add SGD 3,000–7,000/mo. This compresses free cashflow significantly and is the most underestimated variable in this profile.

**Rate rise scenario** — Jump from 1.55% → 4% adds SGD 1,948/mo. Already stress-tested and passes, but consider locking a fixed tranche for payment predictability while the kids are young.

---

**Bottom line:** SGD 2M is comfortably affordable on income (28.6% stress DSR). The purchase works cleanly if CPF OA handles the 20% down payment. Confirm CPF OA balance first, then budget conservatively for childcare before stretching on price.


